  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q24-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "24",
    "prompt": "How many litres of $30\\%$ ethanol solution and how many litres of $60\\%$ ethanol solution must be mixed to produce $18$ litres of $50\\%$ ethanol solution?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "6 litres of $30\\%$ solution and 12 litres of $60\\%$ solution.\n\nEquate the total ethanol in the two solutions to $50\\%$ of 18 litres.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the volume, in litres, of the $30\\%$ solution. The volume of the $60\\%$ solution is $(18-x)$ litres. Equating the volumes of ethanol gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n0.30x+0.60(18-x)&=0.50\\times18\\\\\n0.30x+10.8-0.60x&=9\\\\\n10.8-0.30x&=9\\\\\n0.30x&=1.8\\\\\nx&=6.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe volume of the $60\\%$ solution is $18-6=12$ litres.\n\nCheck: $0.30\\times6+0.60\\times12=9$ litres of ethanol, which is $50\\%$ of 18 litres.\n\nMix 6 litres of $30\\%$ solution with 12 litres of $60\\%$ solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
